  "label": "MCP tools",
  "intent": "A tool is connected over MCP: the two-prong plug seats into its tool port. Light: the plug drives in and its prongs meet the port with a hit; the housing is knocked back by the contact, carrying the plug with it, and both spring back and settle with the plug seated. Strong: the plug is pulled back first, then driven in harder; the housing is knocked further and the pair settle in two beats. Disconnect: the plug is pulled back, dragging the housing a little, then comes free; the housing snaps back with a rebound and the plug settles, fully opaque. Plug and housing stay rigid.",
